//? Title: Native Metaphone context rules
//? Subtitle: Actual consumed spans, emitted bytes and the original twelve word fixtures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A phonetic key compresses a spelling into a rule-based representation that can
group some similar pronunciations. This report specifies datamunge’s actual
byte-oriented Metaphone rules, captures their real context decisions, and
retains the original twelve word examples. It distinguishes reproducible native
outputs from a universal pronunciation model, Unicode normalization or agreement
with every historical Metaphone variant.
)

\toc

> Context, consumption and emitted symbols

Lowercase the original bytes using the active C locale. If the stream begins
with kn,gn,pn,wr or ae, remove its first byte. The canonical producer then scans
the actual resulting stream. A rule can emit zero, one or two working-output
bytes and can consume additional source bytes. Finally uppercase the output. The
trace records actual source spans, lookahead existence, entered top-level
branch, appended working suffix and before/after output lengths.

The retained implementation tests duplicates by comparing the current byte with
the next byte, except cc. Thus it skips the first of equal adjacent bytes rather
than testing the previous emitted symbol. Contexts include retained punctuation
and spaces: a byte that emits nothing can still interrupt adjacency. Initial
vowels, selected vowels after a space and the explicit space rule have their
native conventions. Do not replace this byte contract with an imagined
all-letters preprocessing pass.

The original finite branch rules include ph→f, th→0, selected ch/cia/sh/sio/sia
contexts→x, soft c/g cases, selected silent gh/gn endings and interior x→ks.
Exact captured context/consumption matters: the implemented sign key is S
because its gn branch consumes the n, while the first vowels and space rules
have their own positions. These are native reproducibility facts, not an
assertion that every word’s pronunciation is represented correctly.

> A tiny real digraph consumption

For ph, the actual p branch reads h, consumes the two-byte span and appends
working f. Final case conversion produces F. The diagram and table read that
real single iteration.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/metaphone_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/metaphone.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto t = dm::algorithms::metaphone_trace("ph");
    auto &s = t.steps.front();
    std::print("| actual consumed begin | actual consumed end | current byte | next byte | next exists | " "actual branch | actual working suffix | actual final key |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | " "--- | --- | --- | --- |\n| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",
               s.begin, s.end, unsigned(s.current), unsigned(s.next),
               s.has_next, s.rule, s.emitted, t.analysis.key);
    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    d.node("source", {0, 0},
           std::format("Actual source span\n[{},{}): {}", s.begin, s.end,
                       t.analysis.normalized)).node("branch", {6, 0},
                                                    std::format(
                                                    "Actual {}\nappend {}",
                                                    s.rule, s.emitted)).node(
        "key", {12, 0},
        std::format("Actual final uppercase key\n{}", t.analysis.key)).edge(
        "source", "branch").edge("branch", "key");
    d.save_svg("build/metaphone_tiny.svg");
}
```
