> Retain the original twelve words

The native helper retains
Knight,Wright,Thompson,Xavier,sign,eight,comb,Pneumonia,psychology,Wednesday,Gnome
and phlegm in their original order. The figure compares original byte length
with actual key byte length. A shorter key is simply output compression under
this rule set; the fixtures have no independently labelled pronunciation truth,
so length reduction is not a measure of recognition accuracy.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/metaphone_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/metaphone.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto words = dm::algorithms::metaphone_demo_words();
    std::vector<double> x, input, key;
    std::print("| original word index | original spelling | actual native key | input bytes | actual key " "bytes | actual rule iterations |\n| ---: | --- | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < words.size(); ++i) {
        auto a = dm::algorithms::metaphone_analyze(words[i]);
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", i, words[i], a.key,
                   words[i].size(), a.key.size(), a.iterations);
        x.push_back(i);
        input.push_back(words[i].size());
        key.push_back(a.key.size());
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.points(x, input, "original bytes");
    p.points(x, key, "native key bytes", {124, 58, 237});
    p.x_label("original word index in table order").y_label("actual byte count").title("Original twelve words: native key lengths").save_svg("build/metaphone_original.svg");
}
```
