> Inspect every actual Knight rule

The initial kn cluster removes k, leaving night. The native g branch sees h
followed by consonant t, emits nothing and consumes gh. The trace’s actual
source spans therefore cover the normalized stream without overlap or omission,
while the emitted suffixes concatenate to the lowercase working key. The plotted
counts compare consumed source bytes with appended output bytes at each real
iteration.

Zero lookahead values alone cannot distinguish absence from an embedded NUL. The
trace therefore stores actual lookahead-existence flags as well as byte values.
This makes the byte context inspectable while preserving the native algorithm’s
exact sentinel comparisons.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/metaphone_steps.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/metaphone.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto t = dm::algorithms::metaphone_trace("Knight");
    std::print("Actual normalized stream `{}`; removed onset bytes {}; actual final key `{}`.\n\n| actual " "iteration | consumed begin | consumed end | current byte | next byte | second lookahead " "byte | actual branch | appended bytes | output before | output after |\n| ---: | ---: | " "---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n",
               t.analysis.normalized, t.analysis.onset_removed, t.analysis.key);
    std::vector<double> x, consumed, emitted;
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < t.steps.size(); ++i) {
        auto &s = t.steps[i];
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", i,
                   s.begin, s.end, unsigned(s.current), unsigned(s.next),
                   unsigned(s.next2), s.rule, s.emitted.size(), s.output_before,
                   s.output_after);
        x.push_back(i);
        consumed.push_back(s.end - s.begin);
        emitted.push_back(s.emitted.size());
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.points(x, consumed, "consumed source bytes");
    p.points(x, emitted, "appended key bytes", {22, 163, 74});
    p.x_label("actual context-rule iteration").y_label("actual byte count in that iteration").title("Actual Knight consumption and working emission").save_svg("build/metaphone_steps.svg");
}
```
